Verse 1:
[Db]Savior, [Ab7]like a shepherd [Db]lead us,
[Ab]Much we [Ab7]need Thy tenderest [Db]care;
[Db]In Thy [Ab7]pleasant pastures [Db]feed us,
[Ab]For our [Ab7]use Thy folds pre[Db]pare.
Blessed [Gb]Jesus, blessed [Db]Jesus!
Thou hast [Ab]bought us, Thine we [Db]are.
Blessed [Gb]Jesus, blessed [Db]Jesus!
Thou hast bought us, [Ab7]Thine we [Db]are.

Verse 2:
[Db]We are [Ab7]thine, thou [Db]dost befriend us,
[Ab]be the [Ab7]guardian of [Db]our way;
[Db]keep thy [Ab7]flock, from [Db]sin defend us,
[Ab]seek us [Ab7]when we [Db]go astray.
[Gb]Blessed Jesus, [Db]blessed Jesus!
[Ab]Hear, O hear [Db]us when we pray.
[Gb]Blessed Jesus, [Db]blessed Jesus!
[Ab7]Hear, O hear [Db]us when we pray.

Verse 3:
[Db]Thou hast [Ab7]promised to [Db]receive us,
[Ab]poor and [Ab7]sinful though [Db]we be;
[Db]thou hast [Ab7]mercy to [Db]relieve us,
[Ab]grace to [Ab7]cleanse and [Db]power to free.
[Gb]Blessed Jesus, [Db]blessed Jesus!
[Ab]We will early [Db]turn to thee.
[Gb]Blessed Jesus, [Db]blessed Jesus!
[Ab7]We will early [Db]turn to thee.
